$DIR/main.p:18:6: i holds a view of t (t, line 16), which was given a new value at line 17, so i can no longer be used here
    i looks at memory that t owns, without owning it: the view was made by t at
    line 16. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be used only while
    the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line 17 t was given
    a new value, so the view may look at memory that was released, or at a value
    that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use i before line 17, or give t its new value only after the last use of i
    Or make the view again after line 17:
        i = t
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)

